#: src/Admin/Settings.php:136
msgid "On: a \"Request a return\" link appears next to eligible orders, and the request form is reachable. Off: the link and form disappear from the storefront, existing requests stay in your records. Ships on."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:144
msgid "What can be returned"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:145
msgid "Decide which orders qualify and for how long. An order must clear both tests before its \"Request a return\" link shows."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:149
#: src/Admin/Settings.php:152
msgid "Eligible order statuses"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:163
msgid "Orders in any other status never show the return link. Most shops pick the statuses that mean \"the customer has the goods\", usually Completed (and Processing if you fulfil before marking complete). Ships with Completed and Processing ticked; if you untick everything, Completed is kept so the feature still works."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:168
msgid "Return window (days)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:174
msgid "Applies to Return requests. Counted from the order date. After it passes, the customer can no longer choose Return for that order. Set 0 to accept returns with no deadline. Ships at 30."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s is the date the return window closes.
#: src/Admin/Settings.php:179
#, php-format
msgid "Example: an order placed today can be returned until %s."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:188
msgid "Complaint and repair window (months)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:194
msgid "Applies to Complaint and Repair requests, counted from the order date. A fault can surface long after the return window has closed, and in the EU the legal guarantee runs for at least two years, so this window is separate. Set 0 for no deadline. Ships at 24."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s is the date the complaint and repair window closes.
#: src/Admin/Settings.php:199
#, php-format
msgid "Example: an order placed today can receive a complaint or repair request until %s."
msgstr ""

